  "text": "We present a straightforward model that treats quantum systems as collections of interacting particles and respects symmetry between past and future. This framework offers a tangible picture of the processes occurring in the interval between ordinary measurements, rather than treating that period as a mystery. The symmetry implies that the description works equally well when time is run forward or backward, and it leads to specific predictions about the values obtained from very gentle probing techniques. We examine several ways to understand this time‑balanced view, focusing on the subtle quantities that emerge when the system is only lightly disturbed. The simplest, though somewhat simplistic, reading of the model shows how these gentle probes can be interpreted within the symmetric picture."
